{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PeriodLatticeBasis","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction.uniqueUpToScalar_of_entire_of_sq_not_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction.uniqueUpToScalar_of_entire_of_sq_not_real","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevRigidityReduction.lean#L73-L86","doc":"**Cleaner form — the basis is discharged by the substrate non-degeneracy.**\nGiven `b² ∉ ℝ` (the substrate branch `arg b = π/4`; fails for real `b`), the\nperiod lattice `⟨ib, i/b⟩` is automatically a basis\n(`PeriodLatticeBasis.exists_period_basis`), so Faddeev–Volkov rigidity reduces to\njust **two** open inputs: the two solutions are entire, and the ratio is\n`i/b`-periodic everywhere. (The `ib`-period is still derived from nowhere-zero.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction.uniqueUpToScalar_of_entire","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityReduction.uniqueUpToScalar_of_entire","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevRigidityReduction.lean#L45-L71","doc":"**Reduction of Faddeev–Volkov rigidity to entireness of the two solutions.**\nFor two `FaddeevPhi` solutions `Ψ, Φ` at the same `b` with `Φ` nowhere zero and\nboth entire, `∃ c, Ψ = c·Φ` follows from a basis `bas` of `ℂ` realizing the two\nperiods `⟨ib, i/b⟩` plus the dual `i/b`-periodicity of the ratio. The compact\n`ib`-periodicity is **derived** here (nowhere-zero forces the quasi-period\nprefactor nonzero), then upstream `ratio_const_of_doublyPeriodic` finishes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}